From 05e2398cb59015323b7e6a105fb944c350f3be79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:48:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] net: dwc_eth_qos: add Amlogic T7 glue

The T7 (A311D2) Ethernet MAC is a dwmac 4.x (QoS) core on a 32-bit AXI
port, unlike the 3.x GMAC of G12A/S4 handled by dwmac_meson8b. Add an
Amlogic glue for the dwc_eth_qos driver, matched on amlogic,t7-dwmac:
program PRG_ETH0/PRG_ETH1 for RGMII/RMII with the TX and RX delays from
the device tree (as the Linux dwmac-meson8b G12A code does), enable the
clocks and route the G12A-style MDIO multiplexer to the external PHY.

Tested on the Khadas VIM4 (RTL8211F, 1 Gbit/s): DHCP and ping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
